    <channel>
        <title>DuoUpdater</title>
        <!--
          The Sparkle feed. `scripts/publish-release.sh` regenerates this file on
          every release and pushes it here. The app reads it through
          https://updates.duoupdater.app/appcast.xml (workers/appcast relays this
          file); builds before that read
          https://raw.githubusercontent.com/jizhi0v0/duo-updater/main/appcast.xml
          directly, so this path must keep working.

          Deliberately empty rather than absent: an appcast with no items means
          "nothing newer available", which Sparkle handles as up-to-date, whereas
          a missing file is a fetch error on every check. The first release fills
          it in.

          Release history starts here. Earlier builds were published from a
          separate binary-only repo that existed only while the source was
          private, and are not carried over.
        -->
        <item>
            <title>0.5.26-beta.1</title>
            <pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 00:58:48 +0800</pubDate>
            <link>https://github.com/jizhi0v0/duo-updater/releases/tag/v0.5.26-beta.1</link>
            <sparkle:channel>beta</sparkle:channel>
            <sparkle:version>154</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.5.26-beta.1</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>15.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <sparkle:hardwareRequirements>arm64</sparkle:hardwareRequirements>
            <description sparkle:format="markdown"><![CDATA[**Includes the hotfixes from 0.5.25 alongside the full Beta feature set.**

**Homebrew updates handle compatibility, native installers and multi-app suites more reliably.** A failed metadata refresh keeps existing update offers available for retry.

**Apps display their localized names while existing CLI name selectors keep working.**

**Update All waits when disk space is low.** Space-related automatic-update deferrals can resume after capacity recovers.

**What's New is easier to browse and copy.** Version navigation, keyboard access and a fixed reading header make long release notes easier to follow.

**Codiff, electerm, Suspicious Package, RapidAPI/Paw and Mattermost gain update support.** Supported release tracks keep their own updates and installation checks.

**Leaf version detection remains accurate with newer compiled releases.**
]]></description>
